---
import CaseStudy from '../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';

const facts = [
  { k: 'City', v: 'Brussels' },
  { k: 'Year', v: '2015' },
  { k: 'Homes', v: '29' },
  { k: 'Architects', v: 'stekke + fraas' },
  { k: 'Tenure', v: 'Resident-developed' },
  { k: 'Delivery', v: 'Units as shells' },
  { k: 'Ground floor', v: 'Workspaces' },
];

const gallery = [
  { placeholder: 'Shared garden — photo needed', cap: 'The garden the 29 homes share' },
  { placeholder: 'Shell interior — photo needed', cap: 'A unit at handover: shell now, home later' },
  { placeholder: 'Street front — photo needed', cap: 'Workspaces at the street' },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Brutopia"
  subtitle="Twenty-nine households acting as their own developer."
  heroPlaceholder="Brutopia hero — garden facade (photo needed)"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/sargfabrik/', label: 'Sargfabrik' }}
  next={{ href: '/bijgaardehof/', label: 'Bijgaardehof' }}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-6 pt-16 sm:px-12">
    <p class="text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      Twenty-nine apartments wrap a shared garden in Brussels, with workspaces at the ground floor.
      The residents were the developer: they carried the risk, made the decisions, and kept the
      margin in the building. Units were handed over as shells — structure, envelope, services — and
      finished by each household to its own budget.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      What to steal: the shell. Delivering unfinished interiors is the honest way to hit multiple
      price points in one building without subsidy, and it converts sweat into equity for the
      households who have more time than money.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
    <li>Resident-as-developer removed the margin that makes Bay Area co-ops pencil out red.</li>
    <li>Shells let a mixed-income group build one building instead of two markets.</li>
    <li>
      Ground-floor workspaces are the retail brief's quieter cousin — easier to lease, still eyes on
      the street.
    </li>
    <li>Twenty-nine is enough: Brutopia is Berkeley Scenario 1 at modest scale.</li>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources">
    Sources: project publications by stekke + fraas and the Brutopia cooperative.
  </Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
